WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Retain the inventory. Two fixed six-level banks hold twelve nominal 3U payloads. Select one cell and inhibit host burns during feeding.

2
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Capture the selected payload. The guided pusher feeds the lift. At source level 5 the payload floor is Z830 mm; the lift grips hold its pallet.

3
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Overlap the restraints. At handoff, positive carrier bayonets and outboard lift grip pins establish dual custody. The storage banks and fixed frame are hidden in this view for access.

4
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Prove the clear state. Payload floor Z46 mm. Raised custody frame floor Z190 mm. Prove pallet locks, pusher withdrawal and a clear path before enabling launch.

5
00:00:44.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Retain the pallet during recovery. The payload departs along +X. Carrier and captive pallet arrest together, then return as one retained assembly for the next transfer.

6
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:18.000
Fault → inhibit → retain → verify. Inhibit launch, retain the payload, isolate the cell, supervise reset, then verify before continuing. Physical fault-response validation is subsequent work.
